A person can be elected President if he or she:

- is a **citizen of India**;
- has completed **35 years** of age;
- is **qualified** to be a member of the **Lok Sabha**;
- does **not** hold an **office of profit** under any government. (Being President, Vice-President, Governor or minister does not count.)

All executive action is taken **in the President's name**. The President **appoints**:

- the **Prime Minister**, and other ministers on the PM's advice;
- the **Chief Justice** and judges of the **Supreme Court** and **High Courts**;
- **Governors** of States, the **Attorney General**, the **Comptroller and Auditor General**, the **Election Commissioners**, members of the **UPSC**;
- **ambassadors**; and receives foreign envoys.

The President also runs the **Union Territories** through administrators.
